+## Rulings in wave 2a (1.4.0)
+
+- Ruling R79 (findings 27, 28): one standing (`standingOf`) lists every blocker between a head and its merge, with owner and release, and the guard's refusal and the post-PR prompts render the rest of it after what they already name; a late review is still held by the guard's untriaged-feedback check, with no blocker kind of its own — cost if wrong: longer hold texts.
+- Ruling R80 (amends R62; finding 29): a post waiver covering the head, or naming the PR head the record has not caught up to, ends review holds for it, and `advance` says what it covers instead; a run stopped or waived while a step awaited makes `endRound` do nothing — cost if wrong: a waived head no longer gets a reminder of open findings.
+- Ruling R81 (Adam, decision E): every manual action by the person (`waive pre|post|<id>`, `allow`, `stop`, `reset`, and the pane's Stop) ends with one agent message through `say()`; a note and a prompt the same command queues for the same record become one message, the note's line first, and an agent's own `stop` sends nothing — cost if wrong: one extra message per action.
+- Ruling R82 (amends R32, R34, R36, R40; finding 21; Adam: every unresolved thread gets a reply and/or a fix, as the PR guidance and tool-use hooks required before the gate): triage carries open findings by the round raised in, and `acknowledged` ("asks for no change") counts only with a `replyId`, on a GitHub finding with no security flag and no explicit P0-P2, stored as a rebuttal noted "No change requested:" that Codex checks — cost if wrong: a Codex check for a plain approval note.
+- Ruling R83 (Adam, decision J, narrowed by review G2-2 on PR #19): a review is no finding only on positive no-action evidence (`isNoAction`), and settled reviews are logged as `approval` — cost if wrong: a no-action review the classifier misses goes to triage.
+- Ruling R84 (findings 11, 21): a triaged severity replaces one guessed from a comment's words, up or down, recorded in the history; a reviewer's tag and Codex's severity are never lowered, and a reviewer's advisory label reads as a P3 tag — cost if wrong: an agent lowers a guessed P2 to P3.
+- Ruling R85 (amends R42; Adam, decision I): a P3 deferral with a `followUp`, not security, settles without a waiver — cost if wrong: a P3 the person would have wanted to see.
+- Ruling R86 (amends R1-9; Adam, decision K; finding 28): required checks come from the base's rulesets and classic protection, failing closed when unreadable, and the hold for unreadable CI quotes gh's own error; a post waiver sets aside every other check, named — cost if wrong: a check that should have blocked goes unnoticed under a waiver.
+- Ruling R87 (live use, cookbook PRs #3732 and #3741): a hold on a Bash command that does more than its PR action ends by saying nothing in it ran, and asks for the other steps on their own and the PR command alone; the command is never rewritten to run part of it — cost if wrong: one extra line on a hold.
